#============================================================================

## SECTION 0: SYMBOLS & NOTATION
##
## ⊙ = operation marker (what the dashboard shows)
## → = data flow (from source to display)
## ✓ = spec compliant
## ✗ = spec violated
## τ = timestamp reference
## μ = metric reference
##

---

## DASHBOARD 1: LIVE ELECTIONS (⊙)

Primitive: Meaningful vs Noise — Which elections reflect user decisions vs system ticks?

Data flow:
  ledger_elections.jsonl (all entries)
    → filter: event_type NOT IN {interrupt_timer, boot}
    → select: last 20 meaningful elections ordered by timestamp (descending)
    → display: each as [HH:MM:SS] type → elected (superposition_count)

Output format:
  Live Elections — Real-time Decision Stream

  Total Elections: {total_count}
    Meaningful (user): {user_action_count}
    Noise (timer): {noise_count}

  Recent Decisions:
  [18:23:01] navigate → live_elections  (superposition: 10 options)
  [18:22:58] input_mouse → btn:live-elections  (superposition: 1 option)
  ...

FIELD (Superposition): All elections, meaningful and noise mixed
SELECTION: Filter meaningful only, take recent 20
RECORD: Display as list, include counts and superposition size

Five Gates:
  1. Alignment: Binary choice (meaningful/noise) aligns with election types
  2. Clarity: Filter rule unambiguous (event_type check)
  3. Visibility: Every election visible, timestamps included, all traceable
  4. Kindness: Shows real user decisions, helps understand ARIA's choices
  5. Scaling: Works with 10 elections or 1000 (same algorithm)

Status: ZEROPOINT 18/18 (all gates pass)

---

## DASHBOARD 2: TIMELINE DAG (⊕)

Primitive: Causal chain — Does election B depend on election A via state change?

Data flow:
  ledger_elections.jsonl (all entries, ordered by timestamp)
    → group: by event_type
    → infer: parent = previous election of same or compatible type (heuristic)
    → select: recent 15 elections showing causal sequence
    → display: chronological with implied parent relationships

Output format:
  Timeline DAG — Causal Decision Chain

  Total Elections: {total}
  Event Types: {count}
  Causal Depth (max chain): {depth}

  Chronological Sequence (recent 15):
  → [18:23:01] navigate → live_elections
      (caused_by: input_mouse on btn:live-elections)
  → [18:22:58] input_mouse → btn:live-elections
      (caused_by: user click)
  → [18:22:55] navigate_back → menu
      (caused_by: back button pressed)

  Event Distribution:
    navigate: {n}
    input_mouse: {n}
    navigate_back: {n}
    boot: {n}

FIELD: Election sequence
SELECTION: Group by type, infer causality via sequence, show recent 15
RECORD: Display as chain with parents implied

Five Gates:
  1. Alignment: Causal chain structure aligns with election sequence semantics
  2. Clarity: Parent inference explicit (immediate predecessor of same/related type)
  3. Visibility: Full sequence visible, timestamps included
  4. Kindness: Shows decision flow, helps understand cause-effect
  5. Scaling: Linear O(n) scan, works with any number of elections

Status: ZEROPOINT 18/18 (all gates pass)

---

## DASHBOARD 3: COHERENCE (τ)

Primitive: System health — Is ARIA coherent (metrics healthy) or degraded?

Data flow:
  ledger_coherence_metrics.jsonl (written by kernel each tick)
    → select: latest entry (most recent timestamp)
    → display: all four metrics with percentages
    → show: election count and quality ratio

Output format:
  Coherence Monitoring — System Health

  Consciousness Depth:        {depth:.2f} / 10.0
  Coherence Quality:          {quality:.1%}
  Learning Velocity:          {velocity:.1%}
  Synthesis Convergence:      {synthesis:.1%}

  Election Quality:
    Total Elections:          {total}
    Meaningful Elections:     {meaningful}
    Quality Ratio:            {ratio:.1%}

  System Status:
    Ledger Integrity:         {file_count} files, ALL OK
    Last Update:              {most_recent_timestamp}

FIELD: System metrics in superposition (healthy/degraded)
SELECTION: Read latest metrics entry from ledger
RECORD: Display all four metrics with human-readable labels

Five Gates:
  1. Alignment: Binary (healthy/degraded) aligns with metric thresholds
  2. Clarity: Metrics unambiguous, each has range and interpretation
  3. Visibility: All metrics logged to ledger, history available
  4. Kindness: Shows system wellbeing, helps user understand ARIA state
  5. Scaling: O(1) read, works regardless of metric count

Status: ZEROPOINT 18/18 (all gates pass)

NOTE: Requires new ledger file ledger_coherence_metrics.jsonl
      Written by: ufm_kernel.py in get_frame() method
      Format: One JSON line per write (append-only)

---

## DASHBOARD 4: UTILITIES (◊)

Primitive: Parameter alignment — Is each parameter at spec'd value or deviated?

Data flow:
  ledger_parameters.jsonl (parameter definitions)
    → select: all tunable parameters
    → display: each with current value and allowed range/type
    → show: parameter name, value, type, min/max/options

Output format:
  Utilities — System Parameters

  Tunable Parameters:

    coherence_threshold      0.70       [range: 0.0-1.0]
    election_speed_ms        100        [range: 10-1000]
    allow_backtracking       true       [boolean]
    user_influence_weight    0.50       [range: 0.0-1.0]
    learning_rate            0.10       [range: 0.0-0.5]
    max_superposition        10         [range: 2-50]
    tick_interval_ms         100        [range: 50-500]

  To change: Edit ledger_parameters.jsonl and restart

FIELD: All tunable parameters
SELECTION: Read from ledger, format with current values
RECORD: Display as labeled list with ranges

Five Gates:
  1. Alignment: Parameter structure aligns with system design
  2. Clarity: Each parameter has clear name, type, range
  3. Visibility: All parameters visible, all in ledger
  4. Kindness: Empowers user to tune system behavior
  5. Scaling: Works with any number of parameters

Status: ZEROPOINT 18/18 (all gates pass)

---

## DASHBOARD 5: SYNTHESIS (≡)

Primitive: Integration — Has synthesis/learning occurred or is system baseline?

Data flow:
  ledger_elections.jsonl (all elections)
  + ledger_app_state.jsonl (state history)
    → analyze: event type frequencies, state transitions, visit patterns
    → detect: recurring patterns (navigate often = exploration preference)
    → synthesize: high-level summary of what system learned
    → display: patterns found, most visited views, overall integration status

Output format:
  Synthesis — Integration Status

  ARIA Decision Summary:
    Total Elections Made:     {total}
    User-Initiated:           {user_count}
    System-Initiated:         {system_count}

  Recurring Patterns Detected:
    navigate appears {n} times → strong preference for exploration
    navigate_back appears {m} times → iterative refinement behavior
    [other patterns found]

  Most Visited Dashboards:
    live_elections: {n} visits
    coherence_monitoring: {n} visits
    [others ranked by frequency]

  Integration Status: {summary}
    (Based on decision diversity, learning patterns, state evolution)

FIELD: All elections and state transitions
SELECTION: Aggregate frequencies, detect patterns, rank by recurrence
RECORD: Display summary with pattern descriptions

Five Gates:
  1. Alignment: Pattern detection aligns with election frequency semantics
  2. Clarity: Patterns explicit (visit count → preference inference)
  3. Visibility: All data sources visible, frequencies traceable
  4. Kindness: Shows learning progress, system growth over time
  5. Scaling: Linear aggregation O(n), works with any election count

Status: ZEROPOINT 18/18 (all gates pass)

---

## DASHBOARD 6: FUTURE SIGHT (☆)

Primitive: Prediction — Does next election follow known pattern or is it novel?

Data flow:
  ledger_elections.jsonl (recent 20 meaningful elections)
    → analyze: event_type → elected pairs, compute frequencies
    → predict: most common next action and confidence
    → compare: past predictions vs actual outcomes (accuracy)
    → display: prediction + alternatives + confidence scores

Output format:
  Future Sight — Predictive Analysis

  Based on Recent Decisions (last {n}):

  Most Likely Next Action:
    navigate (confidence: {pct}%)
    Likely target: {most_common_elected_value}

  Alternative Predictions:
    navigate_back (confidence: {pct}%)
    input_mouse (confidence: {pct}%)

  Historical Accuracy:
    Past predictions matched reality: {accuracy:.1%}
    Pattern consistency: {consistency}

  Pattern Detected: {description}
    (e.g., "Strong preference for dashboard exploration")

FIELD: Recent elections in superposition
SELECTION: Most frequent type → elected pairs, compute conditional probabilities
RECORD: Display prediction + confidence + accuracy history

Five Gates:
  1. Alignment: Prediction structure aligns with Markov chain semantics
  2. Clarity: Confidence percentage unambiguous, accuracy computable
  3. Visibility: All predictions logged, comparison against actuals visible
  4. Kindness: Shows system learning patterns, helps understand behavior
  5. Scaling: O(n) histogram, works with any election count

Status: ZEROPOINT 18/18 (all gates pass)

