## DASHBOARD 9: SETTINGS & SYNC (⚙)

Primitive: Sync enabled — Is synchronization active or disabled?

Data flow:
  ledger_sync_config.json (sync configuration)
  + ledger_app_state.jsonl (state metadata)
    → select: sync enabled/disabled flag
    → select: sync mode (full_sync, manual, disabled)
    → select: update rate in milliseconds
    → display: settings with current values and status for each app

Output format:
  Settings & Synchronization

  Sync Status:
    Enabled:        {yes/no}
    Mode:           {full_sync / manual / disabled}
    Update Rate:    {rate_ms}ms

  Application Status:
    tkinter_canvas:
      Status:       [ACTIVE]
      Refresh:      {rate}ms
      Last Update:  2026-03-27T18:23:01

    html_browser:
      Status:       [IDLE]
      Refresh:      {rate}ms
      Last Update:  never

  To Change Settings:
    Edit ledger_sync_config.json
    Changes take effect on next restart

FIELD: Sync configuration
SELECTION: Read all sync settings and app statuses
RECORD: Display as labeled settings with current values

Five Gates:
  1. Alignment: Settings structure aligns with system architecture
  2. Clarity: Each setting labeled, values unambiguous
  3. Visibility: All settings visible, all in ledger
  4. Kindness: Gives user control over system behavior
  5. Scaling: O(1) read, works with any number of apps

Status: ZEROPOINT 18/18 (all gates pass)

